d with her murder was the last  person seen with smart when he walked  her home from the party paul's father  reuben is charged with accessory after  the fact for allegedly helping hide the  body and allegedly burying her in his  backyard and later moving the remains on  wednesday the state continued presenting  its case before two separate juries one  for paul and another for reuben the day  got off to a delayed start as a  scheduled witness fell ill  shelby liddell a forensic specialist  continued her testimony from last week  telling jurors about the excavations of  soil taken from around ruben's home last  year after noticing a change in behavior  from the cadaver dogs  and over in tennessee the man  investigators say abducted and murdered  a memphis mother of two is being held  without bond  thirty-eight-year-old cleotha abstinent  appeared in shelby county court on  wednesday for the second arraignment  this week apston was originally charged  with kidnapping and tampering with  evidence but was later charged with  first degree murder when fletcher's body  was found during wednesday's court  appearance the case's judge revoked  abstinence bond that had previously been  set at five hundred thousand dollars  investigators say 34 year old fletcher  was last seen alive on friday september  2nd just after four o'clock in the  morning officials say she was out for a  run when she was forced into a black suv  and taken away investigators later  confirmed apston was driving that  vehicle he was arrested on saturday and  charged in connection to fletcher's  disappearance on monday memphis area  investigators discovered a body near  where appston was seen cleaning out his  vehicle  on tuesday investigators confirmed that  that body belonged to fletcher so far a  cause of death has not been made public  abstinence due back in court again on  thursday  marie at first bond was set at 500 000  but that was revoked when the murder  charge was added is it common for a  judge 